      "writtenOn": "2026-03-25T14:05:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s some nuance. In chromium, submodules are part of the tree. In other projects, like [webrtc](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/webrtc/.gitignore;l\u003d47;drc\u003deea6b6510b8d6714786b550b009f604e6a538d63) and [v8](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:v8/.gitignore;l\u003d55;drc\u003dfbe8f41e7ce796c07e282d060fbc496e7c220be1), they are gitignored. Both work.\nI\u0027m personally used to having them in-tree, but other people are not and therefore gitignoring avoids mistakes.\nFor instance, in crossbench, submodules became part of the tree [not long ago](crrev.com/c/7031039). Since then we\u0027ve run into cases where people accidentally get them out of sync with DEPS, leading to a dirty tree after `gclient sync`. I fixed a couple of those instances, e.g. crrev.com/c/7531938",
      "parentUuid": "791342fe_acd9a333",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "7af0f813d57f8bdedea95239f02efe2796a96ab1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
