      "writtenOn": "2026-03-23T11:12:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIANM, this is not a standard git command (see [here](https://git-scm.com/docs)). FYI that this would fail the second time a user runs it on their machine unless they manually erase the branch from last time. You could suggest `git branch -f` to force the old branch to the new commit if it exists. Otherwise, to the best of my knowledge, the current command is equivalent to `git branch`.",
      "range": {
